{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779639588,"nonce":"fi9hTrN6HgWOosyP//I4XGxRUfo=","message":"Implementation plan before coding:\n\nI am going to make auth request issue relationships explicit in the auth-owned path rather than treating this as a git-bug special case. The intended steady-state semantics are:\n\n- reference links: context/provenance/dashboard navigation only; never close issues or resolve work units.\n- closure links: explicit resolution targets; closed only after successful auth completion.\n- legacy `issues` payloads remain close-on-merge for compatibility, but new CLI/API names should expose `issue_references` and `issue_closures` so agents do not infer behavior from `--issue`.\n- `Bug:` trailers should be treated as work tracking/reference links, not automatic issue closure. If commit-level closure remains needed, it should use explicit closure trailers such as `Closes:` / `Resolves:`.\n- ledger link types are the durable model: references become `ledger_auth_issue_links.link_type = references`; closures become `resolves`; completion code closes only resolving links.\n\nI will patch the CLI, API/auth queue types, ledger operational-link sync/completion inputs, legacy merge script closure behavior, docs, and focused tests. After that I will audit AGENTS/CLAUDE instructions for stale auth-request guidance and update the relevant project/global files if needed.","files":null}]}